<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71382" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νωλεμές</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without pause, unceasingly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. αἰεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.317
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				17.385
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.191
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ αἰεὶ . . ν. ἐγχρίμπτοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.413
				</span></i>
			 : without 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰεί, μάχην ἀλίαστον ἔχουσι ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.58
				</span></i>
			 ; later, <i>firmly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἐρρίζωθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.605
				</span></i>
			 :—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νωλεμέως</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνον τ᾽ ἐχέμεν καὶ ὀϊζὺν ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.3
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἐχέμεν</span>”
				<i>persevere,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.492
				</span></i>
			 ; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. κτείνοντο</span> they were
			murdered <i>without pause,</i> i.e. one after the other, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.413
			</span></i>.—
				Ep.
			 word, used by <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				5.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.17
			</span></i>.</div>
